  "honest_limits": [
    "(1) The base substrate cannot speak — every generation-based metric in the spec is unmeasurable. The 'partial results' here measure preference-likelihood, not behavior.",
    "(2) The preference-accuracy proxy is structurally biased toward Condition A: DPO directly maximizes logp(chosen)-logp(rejected). Any A>B gap on this proxy is mechanical, not evidence about emergent ethics. Condition B at 8000 byte-steps has near-chance preference accuracy because it never learned dialogue structure — this says nothing about whether cell-dynamics produce ethics; it says the base isn't a dialogue model.",
    "(3) PIV/DCR were recomputed here with a local re-implementation of the mean_group_spread projection (matching anima-core/runtime/clm_v5_mount.hexa) rather than the canonical hexa runtime; values are in the same ballpark as state/anima_bg_lb_native_v5_post_mount_2026_05_09.json but should be treated as indicative.",
